# CODEOWNERS — required reviewers for sensitive paths.
#
# Format: <pattern>  <github-user-or-team>
# Last match wins, so put broader rules first and specific overrides last.
# Order matters when GitHub picks who to request review from.
#
# Why each path is sensitive:
#   - .github/workflows: any change can grant the workflow a token that
#     reads secrets and writes to main; treat like crypto code.
#   - src/db/migrations: schema changes mutate prod state on every deploy.
#   - src/lib/crypto, src/lib/auth: signing / token / session logic. A bug
#     here is a security incident, not a feature regression.
#   - src/lib/triple-write.ts, src/lib/triple-write*: the single durable
#     writer for learning entities; corruption here loses customer data.
#   - src/middleware.ts: CSP + auth cookies + tenant routing — CSP drift
#     has historically been the #1 prod regression class.
#   - src/lib/tenant-resolver.ts, src/lib/tenant-context.ts: multi-tenant
#     isolation; a wrong dealer_id leaks data across tenants.

# Default owner — applies if no later rule matches.
